- id: GameFramework.ConsoleTool
  commentId: N:GameFramework.ConsoleTool
  language: CSharp
  name:
    CSharp: GameFramework.ConsoleTool
    VB: GameFramework.ConsoleTool
  nameWithType:
    CSharp: GameFramework.ConsoleTool
    VB: GameFramework.ConsoleTool
  qualifiedName:
    CSharp: GameFramework.ConsoleTool
    VB: GameFramework.ConsoleTool
  type: Namespace
  assemblies:
  - cs.temp.dll
  modifiers: {}
  items:
  - id: GameFramework.ConsoleTool.Console
    commentId: T:GameFramework.ConsoleTool.Console
    language: CSharp
    name:
      CSharp: Console
      VB: Console
    nameWithType:
      CSharp: Console
      VB: Console
    qualifiedName:
      CSharp: GameFramework.ConsoleTool.Console
      VB: GameFramework.ConsoleTool.Console
    type: Class
    assemblies:
    - cs.temp.dll
    namespace: GameFramework.ConsoleTool
    source:
      id: Console
      path: ''
      startLine: 494
    summary: "\nCore console system that manages command execution, history, and output.\n\nArchitecture:\n- Static class for global access (consider making non-static in future for better testability)\n- Manages command queue, history, and execution\n- Delegates UI operations to registered IConsoleUI implementation\n- Thread-safe command queuing for commands from other threads\n\nCommand Execution Flow:\n1. Commands are queued via EnqueueCommand()\n2. ConsoleUpdate() processes the queue each frame\n3. Commands are tokenized and looked up in registry\n4. Command execution results are output to console\n"
    example: []
    syntax:
      content:
        CSharp: public static class Console
        VB: Public Module Console
    inheritance:
    - System.Object
    inheritedMembers:
